Let $$A = \left( {\matrix{
a & b \cr
c & d \cr

} } \right)$$ where $$a,b,c,d$$ $$ \ne 0$$

$${A^2} = \left( {\matrix{
a & b \cr
c & d \cr

} } \right)\left( {\matrix{
a & b \cr
c & d \cr

} } \right)$$

$$ \Rightarrow {A^2} = \left( {\matrix{
{{a^2} + bc} & {ab + bd} \cr
{ac + cd} & {bc + {d^2}} \cr

} } \right)$$

$$ \Rightarrow {a^2} + bc = 1,\,bc + {d^2} = 1$$

$$ab + bd = ac + cd = 0$$

$$c \ne 0\,\,\,\,\,b \ne 0$$

$$ \Rightarrow a + d = 0 \Rightarrow Tr\left( A \right) = 0$$

$$\left| A \right| = ad - bc = - {a^2} - bc = - 1$$

